Phrase corpus for the shopfront scene
=====================================

Film titles harvested from Wikidata by `scripts/build_phrases.py`, filtered to
those that yield a pun for the trade named in each filename.

Source: Wikidata (https://www.wikidata.org), released under CC0 1.0 Universal.
CC0 requires no attribution; it is recorded here anyway, because a file of
material taken from somewhere should say where.

Only films whose ORIGINAL language is the file's language are included, so the
titles are ones a speaker of that language would recognise rather than
translations of English releases.

These files live in the explorer, which is marked `Private :: Do Not Upload` and
is never published. The `denckring` package itself ships no corpus: ADR 0020
holds that a corpus is supplied by the reader, and `apply` still takes one
phrase from its caller.
